; V7.6 (Package 11 A7a). The Eraser: a Story-only Future Cultist elite of the
; Unbound. The resource ID is "unbound_eraser", not the bare "eraser" the design
; prose uses, because two BOSSES already carry that word - tidal_eraser (L5) and
; apex_eraser (L15, "The First Unbound"). A bare "eraser" would make every grep
; and the VFX library's owner parse ambiguous against them.
;
; Behavior = 0 (Ground) rather than a new "Chase" enum value: the design's Chase
; is the OPPOSITE of StandGuard, which is already the default plus aggro. What
; makes it a hunter is the room-scale aggro pair below - "it ignores siphon-
; defence positioning", so there is no corner of a room it will not cross.
;
; ChronalDustDrop = 10 is INTERIM. The design says the Eraser "draws its authored
; share of the required encounter budget (F05); no flat 20-dust award", but F05's
; reward manifest is A10's and lands in the same wave; 10 is the only value the
; existing elite gate (EnemyRosterContentTests) accepts today. A10 re-points it.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="EnemyData" load_steps=7 format=3]

